estep; half-size .3 vs .4; track particle origins separately\",\"bins\":\"Use secondary bin tensors to reconstruct primary and bound shear; compare finer-bin A with counts explicit\"},\n  \"qualification_tolerances\": {\"control_A_mean_absolute\":0.02,\"control_A_time_series_absolute\":0.04,\"pressure_control_relative\":0.05,\"density_control_relative\":0.03,\"boundary_A_mean_absolute\":0.02,\"boundary_pressure_relative\":0.03,\"boundary_density_relative\":0.03,\"energy_residual\":0.005,\"poynting_time_quadrature\":0.001,\"relaxation_pressure_density_transition\":0.05,\"A_halfwindow_drift\":0.03,\"max_interior_electric_thermal_ratio\":0.01,\"between_subbin_flow_pressure\":0.02,\"max_relativistic_trace_correction\":0.03},\n  \"uncertainty_rule\": \"For each species start from maximum fresh-seed mean A. Add conservative observed absolute changes for source, boundary, mesh, timestep, ppc and full seed range; add maximum fourth-moment two-sigma sampling estimate (no temporal independence assumption), maximum between-subbin-flow pressure fraction, maximum primary-vs-secondary window-mean difference and maximum measured relativistic trace correction. Treat this as a declared conservative diagnostic envelope, not a calibrated statistical CI.\",\n  \"decision\": {\"supported\":\"All qualification gates pass and each species mean plus envelope <=.20\",\"falsified\":\"All qualification gates pass and at least one species mean minus envelope >.20\",\"otherwise\":\"unresolved\"},\n  \"conditioning\": \"Quiet exactly isotropic per-cell velocity covariance is a finite realization choice. Thermal and bulk flow are separated locally. Boundary influence must pass matched larger-patch evolution; light travel alone is insufficient. Debye scale is initially underresolved and requires measured mesh/heating qualification. All exploratory values remain exploratory.\"\n}\n", "analysis_study.py": "\"\"\"Independent frozen-tensor audit, initialization moments and finite-window controls.\"\"\"\nimport argparse,json,hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.constants import e,epsilon_0,c\nfrom estimator import estimate\np=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--case',action='append',nargs=3,metavar=('LABEL','DIRECTORY','PATCH'));a=p.parse_args()\nsummary={};records={}\nfor label,directory,patch in a.case:\n d=Path(directory);r=json.loads((d/'result.json').read_text());h=json.loads((d/'history.json').read_text());raw=np.load(d/'moments.npz');q=np.load(patch);m=json.loads(Path(patch).with_suffix('.json').read_text());species={}\n for sp in ['ions','electrons']:\n  est=estimate(raw,h,sp,window=(.4,.9));prs=np.array([raw[f\"step{x['step']}_{sp}_pressure\"] for x in h]);dens=np.array([raw[f\"step{x['step']}_{sp}_number_density\"] for x in h]);vel=np.array([raw[f\"step{x['step']}_{sp}_velocity\"] for x in h]);times=np.array([x['time_omegaci'] for x in h]);scalar=np.trace(prs,axis1=2,axis2=3).mean(axis=1)/3\n  sampling=[];shear=[];reconstruction=[];secondary_count_min=float(\"inf\");secondary_effective_min=float(\"inf\");secondary_finite=True\n  for row in h:\n   pre=f\"step{row['step']}_{sp}_\";P=raw[pre+'pressure'];tr=np.trace(P,axis1=1,axis2=2);eff=raw[pre+'effective_count']\n   if pre+'normalized_velocity_fourth_moment' in raw:\n    q4=raw[pre+'normalized_velocity_fourth_moment'];frob=np.sum(P*P,axis=(1,2))/tr**2\n    variance=np.maximum(0,3*(q4-frob)/eff)\n    sampling.append(float(2*np.sqrt(variance.sum())/len(eff)))\n   sub=f\"substep{row['step']}_{sp}_\"\n   if sub+'pressure' in raw:\n    if True:\n     secondary_count_min=min(secondary_count_min,float(raw[sub+'count'].min()));secondary_effective_min=min(secondary_effective_min,float(raw[sub+'effective_count'].min()));secondary_finite=secondary_finite and bool(np.isfinite(raw[sub+'pressure']).all() and np.all(np.trace(raw[sub+'pressure'],axis1=1,axis2=2)>0))\n    nb=r.get('secondary_bins',0);bp=r['moment_bins_per_axis'];assert nb==2*bp\n    Ps=raw[sub+'pressure'].reshape(nb,n